      "id": "plans_2026_06_07_household_ui_multi_workspace_plan",
      "label": "Multi-Household Workspaces Plan",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "plans/2026-06-07-household-ui-multi-workspace.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Workspace model (like Slack/Notion) behind the single shared passcode; per-user ownership deferred to the real-auth milestone. The he_household cookie holds the active household id, validated server-side, and is deliberately unsigned because it is not a security boundary. Because all data is already scoped by household_id, once getCurrentHousehold() resolves the active household every view isolates automatically."
    },
    {
      "id": "plans_2026_06_07_household_ui_multi_workspace_rename_technique",
      "label": "Rename-to-Force-Compile-Errors Technique",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "plans/2026-06-07-household-ui-multi-workspace.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Remove the old exported resolver (getDefaultHousehold) and rename it so the type-checker lists every one of the 12 call sites as errors until updated \u2014 guaranteeing completeness, since a missed resolution site would leak data across households."
    }
  ],
